{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MKAUyk4oSLWZNFB3iXEnPk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"PROP-api-request-inv-015\": {\n3\t    \"property_id\": \"PROP-api-request-inv-015\",\n4\t    \"audit_result\": {\n5\t      \"property_id\": \"PROP-api-request-inv-015\",\n6\t      \"classification\": \"potential-vulnerability\",\n7\t      \"code_path\": \"src/api/rolesSync.ts::syncRoles::L25-29\",\n8\t      \"proof_trace\": \"The canonical list endpoint (getAllMembers) correctly applies .is('deleted_at', null) at L18, but syncRoles queries the members table by discord_uid only with no deleted_at filter (L25-29), allowing soft-deleted members to be fetched and operated on. The same codebase applies the filter consistently in getAllMembers and syncAllRoles, confirming the omission in syncRoles is unintentional. updateNickname (nickname.ts L63-67) has the identical missing filter.\",\n9\t      \"attack_scenario\": \"An authenticated API caller posts to POST /api/roles/sync with a soft-deleted member's discord_uid; syncRoles retrieves the deleted member record (no deleted_at guard), and if they remain in the Discord server, re-grants all their original club roles (generation, team, leader, member, verified) — reversing the intended effect of soft-deletion.\",\n10\t      \"checklist_id\": \"PROP-api-request-inv-015\"\n11\t    },\n12\t    \"text\": \"Soft-deleted members (deleted_at != null) must not be accessible via active member queries.\",\n13\t    \"assertion\": \"forall query(active_members): result.every(m => m.deleted_at == null)\",\n14\t    \"covers\": \"SG-001\",\n15\t    \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n16\t    \"type\": \"invariant\"\n17\t  }\n18\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70d65fec-c99e-4b9b-a745-9a613a04cb41","uuid":"45ce0701-6a89-4674-88fa-d90851e5e0f4","timestamp":"2026-04-05T14:37:39.607Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\shieru_k\\Documents\\security-agent\\outputs_stem